  "question": "LATEST CUSTOMER MESSAGE (the one to work on):\ndemo link didnt go out\n\nEARLIER TURNS (context only: they resolve what \"it\", \"that\" or a follow-up refers to while the subject is the same, and do not carry over once the latest message changes subject. Only recent messages are shown and some may be cut, so a detail missing here is not proof the customer never gave it):\nCustomer: Subject: AI SDR misclassifying \"new contact\" auto-replies, blocking replies, and not following up after a booking\n\nHi Acquisity team,\n\nI'm running the Campaign One campaigns (Plumbers, HVAC, Med Spas) in the Company One workspace and found several AI SDR problems this week.\n\n1) Permanent-redirect auto-replies are mislabeled or ignored. Out of roughly 318 threads, I found at least 11 auto-replies in the last 10 days that say a person has left the company and give a replacement contact. Examples: Contact One / Company Two (\"I have taken over Contact One's position, send everything to person-3@domain-3.example\"), Contact Two / Company Three (contact Contact Three), Contact Four / Company Four, Contact Five / Company Five, Contact Six / Company Six, Contact Seven / Company Seven, Contact Eight / Company Eight, Contact Nine / Company Nine (new address given). The AI SDR followed the redirect on only 3 threads (Company Ten, Company Eleven, Company Twelve) and ignored the rest. Contact One's reply was tagged \"Do not contact\" even though the message is a hand-off to a new person.\n\n2) \"Do not contact\" blocks the useful reply. Because that thread is flagged, the inbox shows \"Cannot reply - contains Do not contact emails,\" so I can't forward the intro to Contact Ten. The To field is also locked on every reply, so on any thread I can't change the recipient to the new contact.\n\n3) Categories are too coarse. Auto-replies that redirect to a new contact are being filed under Interested/Auto Reply or Out of Office or Do not contact. Please add a \"Redirect / new contact\" classification, separate from temporary out-of-office and from real opt-outs (\"stop,\" \"unsubscribe,\" \"remove me\").\n\n4) AI SDR is disabled on some of these threads (for example Contact Two and Contact Eleven) and the toggle is greyed out, so I can't turn it back on.\n\n5) After booking a meeting, the AI SDR did not send the demo link. Contact Twelve (Company Thirteen) replied \"Demo\" to a campaign email that promised \"I'l\nSupport: For the Contact Twelve / Company Thirteen thread, what times does your connected calendar show as busy on the day(s) you two discussed for the call, so I can check against what was offered?\nSupport: Thanks, your recording came through. I'm going through it now.\nSupport: For the Contact Twelve / Company Thirteen call, what times does your connected calendar show as busy on the day you two discussed, so I can compare that against the slot that was offered?\nCustomer: the slots offered is fine.. it just didnt send her assets like we said it would\nSupport: Since the booking slots look fine, what exactly did Contact Twelve reply with, or what did she say was missing, so I know which asset (demo link, info packet, etc.) didn't go out?",
